<style>
  /* Rule 0: this is what actually grows the textarea below, in every current browser. */
  .cw-autogrow-demo {
    field-sizing: content;
    min-height: 3lh;
    max-height: 20lh;
    resize: vertical;
    width: 100%;
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }
</style>

<%= cw.autogrow_for max_rows: max_rows do |a| %>
  <textarea <%= cw_attrs(a.root_attrs, class: "cw-autogrow-demo") %> rows="1">Type past one line and this box grows. That is the CSS class above, not cw--autogrow — open dev tools and you will find data-controller="cw--autogrow" on this element, but its connect() returns immediately the moment it detects CSS.supports("field-sizing", "content"), which every current browser reports true for.</textarea>
<% end %>

<p>
  <code>cw--autogrow</code> is wired up above purely to prove it stays a safe, inert no-op
  next to the CSS — not because it is doing any of the visible work.
</p>
